  "name": "Rock beur (Franco-Maghrebi rock of the 1980s)",
  "family": "rock",
  "lineage": "French rock of the 1980s made by the children of North African immigrants, above all around Lyon, where the band Carte de Sejour, fronted by Rachid Taha, formed at the start of the decade and sang in Arabic and French over punk and new-wave rock laced with North African melody. Its 1986 version of Charles Trenet's Douce France, released amid the anti-racist movement of the period, became an emblem of the beur generation.",
